                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It’s hard—really hard. It can easily get frustrating. Yet, it’s still quite inviting—mildly charismatic, though not overly so. It’s far from a casual experience, even though a casual mode exists. This game is for those who want a challenge and have plenty of time to sink into it. If you’re looking for a narrative-driven experience where you can immerse yourself in the game world and get to know the characters deeply, stay far away from this one. But if you’re a masochist and the mere mention of *La-Mulana* gives you a hard-on, then this game is for you. It’s vastly easier than *La-Mulana* tho, but vastly harder than *Blasphemous*.",
